  "notes": "Re-split: 90-91 (from 87-91) joined to 92-94, because the reciter joins 90-91-92 without a pause. Nothing drawn for the Fire or the gold ransom (91:13: no coins or gold motif); an hourglass for dying in disbelief. 90:9-11 «لن تقبل توبتهم» is not glossed: Al-Muyassar (at death) and As-Sa'di (they are not granted repentance) differ. 91: short-word flag at 15 (listen). A jewel for what one loves, wheat for the food, a scroll for the Torah; no motif on Ya'qub (Israil). 92:1-3 uses As-Sa'di's general «البر» (Al-Muyassar narrows it to Paradise)."
 },
